startup-time-checker (1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: call /usr/bin/date by absolute path with a clean environment
    from the setuid binary (PATH hijack gave root).
  * Non-root users may only extend an active lock; add root-only "clear".
  * Compare lock times as Unix seconds so DST/offset changes cannot break
    the check; never block boot on a missing or corrupt state file.
  * Write the state file atomically.
  * Add go.mod targeting Go 1.27; offline module-mode build.
  * Packaging: debhelper-compat 14, Rules-Requires-Root: no, systemd unit in
    /usr/lib via dh_installsystemd (ordered after local-fs and time-set),
    setuid bit via dh_fixperms, copyright, source format, lintian overrides,
    purge removes the state file, build-time tests.

 -- Ulf Karlsson <karlsson.ulf@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0100

